{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e04-scene-19",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Обед для персонала  (Staff Lunch)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "max": "Макс",
  "senya": "Сеня"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The staff are hungry, and Max is in charge of lunch. Senya asks when it will be ready, and Max promises a special soup that is nothing like the usual slop. Here's the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Макс, мы сегодня обедать будем?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно, всё уже почти готово!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы все очень хотим есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Подождите ещё пару минут.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Что ты нам приготовил сегодня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я сварил особенный суп-пюре.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Обычный суп был бы лучше.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вы все пальчики оближете!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Надеюсь, это можно есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вы такого никогда не пробовали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Главное, чтобы было вкусно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Это не то обычное месиво.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ладно, неси скорее на стол!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сейчас я вас всех удивлю!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now the wait for lunch.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Макс, мы сегодня обедать будем?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Max, are we going to have lunch today?' \"Obedat'\" is \"to have lunch\", from \"obed\". Senya puts it before \"budem\", we will, which stresses lunch.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно, всё уже почти готово!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Of course, everything is already almost ready!' \"Pochti\" is \"almost\". \"Gotovo\" ends in -o to agree with \"vsyo\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы все очень хотим есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We all really want to eat.' \"Khotim yest'\", we want to eat, is the usual way to say \"we're hungry\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Подождите ещё пару минут.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Wait a couple more minutes.' \"Podozhdite\" is \"wait\" for several people. \"Yeshchyo paru minut\" is \"another couple of minutes\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Что ты нам приготовил сегодня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What did you prepare for us today?' \"Nam\", to us, does the job of \"for us\". \"Prigotovil\" is the man's \"prepared\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я сварил особенный суп-пюре.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I cooked a special purée soup.' \"Svaril\" is \"varit'\", to boil, with \"s-\" for finished. \"Sup-pyure\" is a borrowed compound.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Обычный суп был бы лучше.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A regular soup would be better.' \"By\" is the little word for \"would\": \"byl by luchshe\", would be better.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вы все пальчики оближете!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You will all lick your fingers!' \"Pal'chiki oblizhete\" is \"you'll lick your little fingers\", the Russian for finger-licking good.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Надеюсь, это можно есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I hope this is edible.' \"Nadeyus'\", I hope, shares a root with \"nadezhda\", hope. \"Mozhno yest'\" is \"it's possible to eat\", meaning edible.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вы такого никогда не пробовали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You have never tasted such a thing.' \"Nikogda ne probovali\" doubles the negative. After it, \"takoye\" becomes the \"of\" form \"takogo\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Главное, чтобы было вкусно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The main thing is that it is tasty.' \"Chtoby\" is \"so that\", and the verb after it goes into the past: \"chtoby bylo vkusno\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Это не то обычное месиво.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is not that usual slop.' \"Mesivo\", slop, is from \"mesit'\", to knead. \"Obychnoye\", usual, is neuter to match.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ладно, неси скорее на стол!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Alright, bring it quickly to the table!' \"Nesi\" is \"carry\", from \"nesti\". \"Na stol\" is \"onto the table\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сейчас я вас всех удивлю!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Now I will surprise you all!' \"Udivlyu\", I'll surprise, has \"divo\", a marvel, at its root. \"Vas vsekh\" is \"all of you\". Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Макс, мы сегодня обедать будем?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно, всё уже почти готово!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы все очень хотим есть.",
   "gap": 0.5
